{type:"pressHome",path:"/press"},{type:"press",path:"/press/:uid"},{type:"blogHome",path:"/news"},{type:"blog",path:"/news/:uid"},{type:"faq-page",path:"/faqs/:subpath2?/:uid",resolvers:{subpath2:"subpath2"}},{type:"landing-page",path:"/:uid"},{type:"content-page",path:"/:subpath1?/:subpath2?/:uid",resolvers:{subpath1:"subpath1",subpath2:"subpath2"}}]},preview:"/preview",toolbar:true,imports:["vue"],components:{richTextComponents:"~/prismic/richTextComponents"}}},app:{baseURL:"/",buildId:"7e544b5a-0a75-4bc7-b691-fdfd0ac7333b",buildAssetsDir:"/_nuxt/",cdnURL:""}}</script><script type="application/json" data-nuxt-data="nuxt-app" data-ssr="true" id="__NUXT_DATA__">[["ShallowReactive",1],{"prerenderedAt":2,"data":3,"state":206,"once":13511,"_errors":13512,"serverRendered":86,"path":13514,"pinia":13515},1784019912274,["ShallowReactive",4],{"content-page-subpath1:how-to-label-a-parcel":5,"page-header-video-undefined":30},{"uid":6,"document":7,"postSlices":205},"how-to-label-a-parcel",{"titleTag":8,"metaDescription":9,"canonical":10,"subpath1":11,"subpath2":22,"slices":23},"How to Label a Parcel in The UK | Labelling Parcels | Evri","Are you sending a package? You’ll need to know how to label your parcel properly. Here's everything you need to know about labelling your packages with Evri.","how-to-label-a-parcel.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Fhow-to-label-a-parcel",{"id":12,"type":13,"tags":14,"lang":16,"slug":17,"first_publication_date":18,"last_publication_date":18,"uid":17,"link_type":19,"key":20,"isBroken":21},"ZL-1EREAACAAEkhR","subpath1",[15],"Guides","en-gb","guides","2023-07-25T12:59:36+0000","Document","0a7b079a-469d-476f-9346-88b7957d3cd5",false,{"link_type":19},[24,52,77,142,158],{"variation":25,"version":26,"items":27,"primary":29,"id":50,"slice_type":51,"slice_label":30},"pageHeaderNoCta","sktwi1xtmkfgx8626",[28],{},{"theme":30,"PageHeaderTitle":31,"PageHeaderText":32,"PageHeaderImage":37,"heroImage":48,"videoContent":49,"showPremiumLogo":30},null,"How to label a parcel",[33],{"type":34,"text":35,"spans":36},"paragraph","Learn how to label your parcel correctly with Evri",[],{"dimensions":38,"alt":41,"copyright":30,"url":42,"id":43,"edit":44},{"width":39,"height":40},500,132,"Send a parcel","how-to-label-a-parcel.html\u002F\u002Fev-mercury.cdn.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002Fbe2c756c-941a-4d5c-9ee4-e588846e0298_send-landing.svg","YiExBxIAACgAAWmC",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":47},0,1,"#fff",{},{"link_type":19},"page_header$685be352-9a1d-4aca-9374-66032117e119","page_header",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":54,"primary":56,"id":75,"slice_type":76,"slice_label":30},"cardWithImageNoCta",[55],{},{"CardImage":57,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":67,"CardText":68,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":58,"alt":61,"copyright":30,"url":62,"id":63,"edit":64},{"width":59,"height":60},1000,667,"An older man is cutting out a label. Only his hands are visible.","how-to-label-a-parcel.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6oyP5bqstJ9-cWm_EVRI_LOCATION_06_10756.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6oyP5bqstJ9-cWm",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"transparent","none","Labelling an Evri parcel",[69,72],{"type":34,"text":70,"spans":71},"If you’re selling lots of things online or giving regular gifts to your friends, chances are you’ll probably need to send a lot of parcels. But did you know there’s a right way when it comes to how to label a parcel properly?",[],{"type":34,"text":73,"spans":74},"To make sending your next batch of packages that much easier, here are top tips on how to label a parcel with Evri for when you next need to use our services.",[],"card$2f808ba1-077e-478c-934b-45e7637da718","card",{"variation":78,"version":26,"items":79,"primary":137,"id":140,"slice_type":141,"slice_label":30},"default-slice",[80,89,97,105,113,121,129],{"title":81,"content":82,"isNumbered":86,"icon":87,"image":88},"Remove any old labels from your box",[83],{"type":34,"text":84,"spans":85},"Whether you’re using a newly bought box, a recycled parcel, or sending a return, make sure you remove any old parcel labels, to avoid any confusion for our team.",[],true,{},{},{"title":90,"content":91,"isNumbered":86,"icon":95,"image":96},"Position your label in the correct position",[92],{"type":34,"text":93,"spans":94},"If your parcel has flat sides, you’ll need to position your label in the middle of its top. For round parcels, simply stick your label where you have enough room.",[],{},{},{"title":98,"content":99,"isNumbered":86,"icon":103,"image":104},"Make sure the label sits flat",[100],{"type":34,"text":101,"spans":102},"Your label needs to be clearly visible and shouldn’t bend around the corners of your parcel. This makes it easily readable and ensures its barcode can be read by our scanners. ",[],{},{},{"title":106,"content":107,"isNumbered":86,"icon":111,"image":112},"Tape your label securely",[108],{"type":34,"text":109,"spans":110},"Be careful to secure your label properly so it can’t get lost in transit. You can do this by applying a strip of parcel tape to each of its edges, making sure not to leave any paper exposed.",[],{},{},{"title":114,"content":115,"isNumbered":86,"icon":119,"image":120},"Don’t obscure your label",[116],{"type":34,"text":117,"spans":118},"This can make reading the address harder, and you want its barcode to be as easy to scan as possible.",[],{},{},{"title":122,"content":123,"isNumbered":86,"icon":127,"image":128},"Don’t place your parcel label inside your package",[124],{"type":34,"text":125,"spans":126},"Your parcel label should always be on the front of your package. ",[],{},{},{"title":130,"content":131,"isNumbered":86,"icon":135,"image":136},"Don’t stick your parcel label over the package edges",[132],{"type":34,"text":133,"spans":134},"This is to make it easily scannable, but you’ll also want to make sure you tape up your parcel so that the edges don’t open up in transit.",[],{},{},{"theme":30,"title":138,"description":139,"showPaddingTop":21},"How to label a parcel in the UK","Label placement is very important when prepping your parcel for delivery, so that it enjoys a quick and direct journey to its destination. We recommend taking the following steps when applying your label:","list_block$10ef69dc-5d04-46ce-87eb-76e70ccfd61a","list_block",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":143,"primary":145,"id":157,"slice_type":76,"slice_label":30},[144],{},{"CardImage":146,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":152,"CardText":153,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":147,"alt":148,"copyright":30,"url":149,"id":150,"edit":151},{"width":59,"height":60},"Customer sat at a desk unpeeling a printed delivery label to place onto the parcel in front of them.","how-to-label-a-parcel.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6R6EJbqstJ9-ST7_EVRI_LOCATION_05_8647.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6R6EJbqstJ9-ST7",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"Should you include your return address?",[154],{"type":34,"text":155,"spans":156},"Yes, just write your address on a return label, then stick it on the back of the parcel you’re sending. Ensure you write “return address” above, to make it clear. If you want to be doubly sure your recipient can return your package, you can always leave a second copy of your return address inside your package.",[],"card$d30df186-73e2-4640-8038-84a857d6397c",{"variation":78,"version":26,"items":159,"primary":161,"id":204,"slice_type":76,"slice_label":30},[160],{},{"CardImage":162,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":168,"CardText":169,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":202,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":163,"alt":164,"copyright":30,"url":165,"id":166,"edit":167},{"width":59,"height":60},"A close-up of a customer's hands as they are crouched on the floor, applying a label to their parcel. They are surrounded by lots of parcels.","how-to-label-a-parcel.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6XsXpbqstJ9-Wex_EVRI_LOCATION_04_5263.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6XsXpbqstJ9-Wex",{"x":4